{"retrieved_on": "2026-11-13", "source_url": "https://www.ebi.ac.uk/europepmc/webservices/rest/search?query=%28EXT_ID%3A31178118+OR+EXT_ID%3A31199919+OR+EXT_ID%3A31209238+OR+EXT_ID%3A31214791+OR+EXT_ID%3A31217097+OR+EXT_ID%3A31217225+OR+EXT_ID%3A31222375+OR+EXT_ID%3A31226704+OR+EXT_ID%3A31231720+OR+EXT_ID%3A31240330+OR+EXT_ID%3A31243334+OR+EXT_ID%3A31263116+OR+EXT_ID%3A31270850+OR+EXT_ID%3A31270976+OR+EXT_ID%3A31283474+OR+EXT_ID%3A31296975+OR+EXT_ID%3A31307017+OR+EXT_ID%3A31308507+OR+EXT_ID%3A31313636+OR+EXT_ID%3A31315618+OR+EXT_ID%3A31317118+OR+EXT_ID%3A31320621+OR+EXT_ID%3A31322692+OR+EXT_ID%3A31332558+OR+EXT_ID%3A31350588+OR+EXT_ID%3A31354393+OR+EXT_ID%3A31355445+OR+EXT_ID%3A31363513+OR+EXT_ID%3A31388413+OR+EXT_ID%3A31399699+OR+EXT_ID%3A31410221+OR+EXT_ID%3A31417138+OR+EXT_ID%3A31419814+OR+EXT_ID%3A31444548+OR+EXT_ID%3A31446280+OR+EXT_ID%3A31450799+OR+EXT_ID%3A31463251+OR+EXT_ID%3A31463368+OR+EXT_ID%3A31466046+OR+EXT_ID%3A31466261+OR+EXT_ID%3A31468205+OR+EXT_ID%3A31473947+OR+EXT_ID%3A31481890+OR+EXT_ID%3A31495281+OR+EXT_ID%3A31504423+OR+EXT_ID%3A31522983+OR+EXT_ID%3A31523482+OR+EXT_ID%3A31527658+OR+EXT_ID%3A31537986+OR+EXT_ID%3A31549948+OR+EXT_ID%3A31561183+OR+EXT_ID%3A31561209+OR+EXT_ID%3A31573400+OR+EXT_ID%3A31585960+OR+EXT_ID%3A31591062+OR+EXT_ID%3A31592346+OR+EXT_ID%3A31592444+OR+EXT_ID%3A31597914+OR+EXT_ID%3A31601480+OR+EXT_ID%3A31603772%29+AND+SRC%3AMED&format=json&resultType=core&pageSize=100", "hitCount": 1, "resultList": {"result": [{"id": "31270850", "source": "MED", "pmid": "31270850", "pmcid": "PMC6771733", "fullTextIdList": {"fullTextId": ["PMC6771733"]}, "doi": "10.1002/sim.8281", "title": "The Integrated Calibration Index (ICI) and related metrics for quantifying the calibration of logistic regression models.", "authorString": "Austin PC, Steyerberg EW.", "authorList": {"author": [{"fullName": "Austin PC", "lastName": "Austin", "firstName": "Peter C", "initials": "PC", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3337-233X"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "ICES, Toronto, Canada."}, {"affiliation": "Institute of Health Management, Policy and Evaluation, University of Toronto, Toronto, Canada."}, {"affiliation": "Sunnybrook Research Institute, Toronto, Canada."}]}}, {"fullName": "Steyerberg EW", "lastName": "Steyerberg", "firstName": "Ewout W", "initials": "EW", "authorId": {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7787-0122"}, "authorAffiliationDetailsList": {"authorAffiliation": [{"affiliation": "Department of Public Health, Erasmus University Medical Center, Rotterdam, The Netherlands."}, {"affiliation": "Department of Biomedical Data Sciences, Leiden University Medical Centre, Leiden, The Netherlands."}]}}]}, "authorIdList": {"authorId": [{"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0002-7787-0122"}, {"type": "ORCID", "value": "0000-0003-3337-233X"}]}, "dataLinksTagsList": {"dataLinkstag": ["altmetrics"]}, "journalInfo": {"issue": "21", "volume": "38", "journalIssueId": 2846986, "dateOfPublication": "2019 Sep", "monthOfPublication": 9, "yearOfPublication": 2019, "journal": {"medlineAbbreviation": "Stat Med", "title": "Statistics in medicine", "essn": "1097-0258", "issn": "0277-6715", "nlmid": "8215016", "isoabbreviation": "Stat Med"}, "printPublicationDate": "2019-09-01"}, "pubYear": "2019", "pageInfo": "4051-4065", "abstractText": "Assessing the calibration of methods for estimating the probability of the occurrence of a binary outcome is an important aspect of validating the performance of risk-prediction algorithms. Calibration commonly refers to the agreement between predicted and observed probabilities of the outcome. Graphical methods are an attractive approach to assess calibration, in which observed and predicted probabilities are compared using loess-based smoothing functions. We describe the Integrated Calibration Index (ICI) that is motivated by Harrell's E<sub>max</sub> index, which is the maximum absolute difference between a smooth calibration curve and the diagonal line of perfect calibration. The ICI can be interpreted as weighted difference between observed and predicted probabilities, in which observations are weighted by the empirical density function of the predicted probabilities. As such, the ICI is a measure of calibration that explicitly incorporates the distribution of predicted probabilities. We also discuss two related measures of calibration, E50 and E90, which represent the median and 90th percentile of the absolute difference between observed and predicted probabilities. We illustrate the utility of the ICI, E50, and E90 by using them to compare the calibration of logistic regression with that of random forests and boosted regression trees for predicting mortality in patients hospitalized with a heart attack. The use of these numeric metrics permitted for a greater differentiation in calibration than was permissible by visual inspection of graphical calibration curves.", "affiliation": "ICES, Toronto, Canada.", "publicationStatus": "ppublish", "language": "eng", "pubModel": "Print-Electronic", "pubTypeList": {"pubType": ["Research Support, Non-U.S. Gov't", "research-article", "Journal Article", "Research Support, N.I.H., Extramural"]}, "grantsList": {"grant": [{"agency": "Canadian Institutes of Health Research", "grantId": "CRT43823", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "CIHR", "grantId": "CTP79847", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Canadian Institutes of Health Research", "grantId": "MOP 86508", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Heart and Stroke Foundation of Canada", "grantId": "Mid‐Career Investigator Award", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Patient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute", "grantId": "ME‐1606‐35555", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "CIHR", "grantId": "MOP 86508", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Patient-Centered Outcomes Research Institute", "grantId": "SA.Tufts.PARC.OSCO.2018.01.25", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Ontario Ministry of Health and Long-Term Care", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NINDS NIH HHS", "acronym": "NS", "grantId": "U01 NS086294", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "NIH HHS", "acronym": "NH", "grantId": "U01NS086294", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "CIHR", "grantId": "CRT43823", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "Canadian Institutes of Health Research", "grantId": "CTP79847", "orderIn": 0}, {"agency": "National Institutes of Health", "grantId": "U01NS086294", "orderIn": 0}]}, "meshHeadingList": {"meshHeading": [{"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Humans"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Logistic Models"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Monte Carlo Method"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "descriptorName": "Probability"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Risk Assessment", "meshQualifierList": {"meshQualifier": [{"majorTopic_YN": "Y", "abbreviation": "MT", "qualifierName": "methods"}]}}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Algorithms"}, {"majorTopic_YN": "N", "descriptorName": "Computer Simulation"}]}, "keywordList": {"keyword": ["Logistic regression", "Model validation", "calibration"]}, "subsetList": {"subset": [{"code": "IM", "name": "Index Medicus"}]}, "fullTextUrlList": {"fullTextUrl": [{"availability": "Subscription required", "availabilityCode": "S", "documentStyle": "doi", "site": "DOI", "url": "https://doi.org/10.1002/sim.8281"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "html", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC6771733"}, {"availability": "Open access", "availabilityCode": "OA", "documentStyle": "pdf", "site": "Europe_PMC", "url": "https://europepmc.org/articles/PMC6771733?pdf=render"}]}, "isOpenAccess": "Y", "inEPMC": "Y", "inPMC": "Y", "citedByCount": 220, "hasReferences": "Y", "hasTextMinedTerms": "Y", "hasDbCrossReferences": "N", "hasPDF": "Y", "hasBook": "N", "hasSuppl": "N", "hasLabsLinks": "Y", "hasData": "N", "license": "cc by-nc-nd", "authMan": "N", "epmcAuthMan": "N", "nihAuthMan": "N", "hasTMAccessionNumbers": "N", "dateOfCompletion": "2021-01-11", "dateOfCreation": "2019-07-05", "dateO